cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite this software release and the associated
  CEDDAR manuscript.
type: software
title: 'CEDDAR: Controllable Ensemble Diffusion Downscaling for Atmospheric Rainfall'
version: 1.1.0
doi: '10.5281/zenodo.23373100'
date-released: '2026-10-14'
authors:
  - family-names: Quistgaard
    given-names: Thea
repository-code: 'https://github.com/TheaQG/CEDDAR'
url: 'https://github.com/TheaQG/CEDDAR'
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  Conditional diffusion-based downscaling of daily ERA5 precipitation to
  DANRA-scale precipitation over Denmark. Software v1.1.0 accompanies the revised
  GMD manuscript and includes the audited sigma-star implementation fixes,
  revised evaluation framework and manuscript figure workflow. The manuscript's
  model identity remains CEDDAR v1.0.2; trained weights and architecture are
  unchanged. Derived manuscript figure data are archived on Zenodo at
  https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23369324.
keywords:
  - precipitation downscaling
  - diffusion models
  - ensemble generation
  - model evaluation
  - reproducibility
